{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/766077-discipline-failure-and-successive-attempts","id":766077,"title":"Discipline Failure and Successive Attempts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-14T23:02:18-08:00","id":766077,"title":"Discipline Failure and Successive Attempts","content":"In my session last night, one of the vampires tried to Mesmerize a police officer and failed. He promptly attempted to do so again. The officer had no reason to suspect his mind was being tampered with, and the failure description for mesmerize says nothing about the victim realizing what you're doing or you being unable to try again.<br /> <br /> So, I ruled that he could essentially keep trying until it worked.<br /> <br /> It worked on his second roll, but looking back on that, it seems a little...off to me. Have I missed a rule somewhere that would prevent him from just trying his discipline over and over until it worked?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-14T23:12:52-08:00","id":766082,"title":"","content":"Successive Attempts, under Permutations of rolling dice on page 173, is the general rule. <i>(That's for the 2e Vampire rulebook \u2013 the same rule is found in the 1e World of Darkness rulebook on p. 132.)</i> If you have no pressing factors \u2013 all the time you need, nobody creeping down your back, no pressure to avoid getting caught or whatever \u2013 then you can just roll your dice pool repeatedly, taking however much time an attempt takes each time. If there's some kind of tension involved, your dice pool shrinks cumulatively for every attempt after the first, until you're down to a chance die.<br /> <br /> The use of a Discipline probably ought to default to posing some risk of being found out, at least, as noted on p. 125 under Using Disciplines: even when you try to activate a Discipline and fail, invoking the Beast still evokes some kind of minor spookiness. A single flicker in the lights is innocuous. But if the lights flicker, then there's a brief, odd chill, then the window glass fogs up, then he's not sure but he thought he saw your eyes twitch unnaturally for a moment... well, the whole is greater than the sum of its parts. I say &quot;default&quot; because there might be times when the use of a Discipline just doesn't have any dramatic tension and you should just let the dude succeed and move on. But a lot of Discipline uses might be more interesting with that tension. How far are you willing to press it to make this work?<br /> <br /> <b>Edit:</b> <i>Whoops, forgot edition wasn't specified. Added the 1e Successive Attempts citation, rule's the same in both editions. I'm not sure whether the spooky SFX of Discipline use were in first edition; still makes sense from a dramatic standpoint to judge when there ought to be tension and when just to let it go.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","user":"Stupid Loserman","date":". 11-15-2015, 02:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-15T12:27:27-08:00","id":766461,"title":"","content":"The cop might find it a little weird that the character keeps trying to lock eyes with him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}